WEBVTT

00:00:04.754 --> 00:00:06.630
[TOY TRAIN HORN WHISTLING] [SMOOCHES]

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.758
You handled that very well, Peter.

00:00:08.758 --> 00:00:12.762
Contrite, apologetic and even a little bit remorseful.

00:00:12.762 --> 00:00:14.931
I'm sorry. What? Oh.

00:00:14.931 --> 00:00:17.474
I put these in for when I'm feeling misunderstood.

00:00:17.474 --> 00:00:21.478
Oh, come on, Peter. Sometimes you have to face the music.

00:00:21.478 --> 00:00:23.981
And these are for when I'm feeling ganged up on.

00:00:23.981 --> 00:00:26.525
You always take things one step too far.

00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:29.279
I'm sorry. What?

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:32.198
What's this? Basil-Jones Publishing.

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:34.658
We carried a section of their books at Harrods.

00:00:34.658 --> 00:00:37.412
It was the last display I arranged before I resigned.

00:00:37.412 --> 00:00:40.123
You mean, fired and physically removed from the store.

00:00:40.123 --> 00:00:41.707
Potato, "potahto."

00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:44.877
It's from Nigel Basil-Jones himself.

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:47.504
He wants to publish my book.

00:00:47.504 --> 00:00:49.924
No. Uh, get it in every bookstore,

00:00:49.924 --> 00:00:52.051
promote it, put it in different languages.

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:54.678
That's incredible. Bea, you've done it.

00:00:54.678 --> 00:00:56.180
This is it. It's happening!

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:57.765
[BEA & THOMAS LAUGHING]

00:00:57.765 --> 00:00:59.016
Promise me something.

00:00:59.016 --> 00:01:00.810
When this book is a huge success,

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:02.353
you'll keep me humble.

00:01:02.353 --> 00:01:05.481
The book is about all of us. Oh! Thank you.

00:01:05.481 --> 00:01:06.941
You're already doing it.

00:01:06.941 --> 00:01:08.192
Dink!

00:01:08.192 --> 00:01:10.403
[♪♪♪]

00:01:12.947 --> 00:01:14.073
[HUMMING]

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:15.241
Why do you always copy

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.826
everything I do?

00:01:16.826 --> 00:01:19.787
Fine. I'll do something different.

00:01:19.787 --> 00:01:20.913
Ow! Ooh, sorry.

00:01:20.913 --> 00:01:23.124
Anyone hungry? Yeah, starving.

00:01:23.124 --> 00:01:25.293
PETER: Leave it with me.

00:01:25.293 --> 00:01:27.086
[FLIES BUZZING]

00:01:29.672 --> 00:01:31.257
[GRUNTS]

00:01:32.842 --> 00:01:35.470
Okay, take one bite and pass it around.

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:37.680
I'm just going to wait until we get home,

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:39.974
where the food isn't decomposing.

00:01:39.974 --> 00:01:42.601
Yeah. Yeah, me too.

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:44.561
Well, la-di-da.

00:01:44.561 --> 00:01:48.399
I didn't realize I was with a bunch of sophisticates.

00:01:49.859 --> 00:01:51.735
[GAGS]

00:01:51.735 --> 00:01:52.945
[GAGS]

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.032
[RETCHES]

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:00.495
[BRAKES SCREECHING]

00:02:02.246 --> 00:02:05.124
MOPSY: Let's go get some dinner. RABBITS: Yeah! Woo-hoo!

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:06.376
[PANTING]

00:02:08.752 --> 00:02:10.171
THOMAS: And there they go.

00:02:10.171 --> 00:02:11.506
Right through the opening

00:02:11.506 --> 00:02:13.466
where there once was a gate.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.634
Good for them. Do they do any of the planting

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:17.761
and weeding and watering? No, they don't.

00:02:17.761 --> 00:02:20.597
But they were here first. BEA: Exactly.

00:02:20.597 --> 00:02:23.267
And you still have your tomatoes.

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:25.395
My tomatoes. Heh-heh.

00:02:25.395 --> 00:02:27.688
I would never have thought a city man

00:02:27.688 --> 00:02:29.648
would like to garden that much.

00:02:29.648 --> 00:02:33.110
I even heard he wants to try and sell them at market.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:37.573
Hm, it's too moist. I'll get the hair dryer.

00:02:37.573 --> 00:02:39.700
It's about time he had a hobby.

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:42.619
I hope he's as successful at his as I am at mine.

00:02:42.619 --> 00:02:44.038
And what is that?

00:02:44.038 --> 00:02:45.831
Passing judgment.

00:02:45.831 --> 00:02:50.378
What is going on with her hair?

00:02:50.378 --> 00:02:52.171
[BOTH PANTING]

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:54.715
Wait! You don't have to try to eat me anymore.

00:02:54.715 --> 00:02:57.134
Remember? You're welcome to all of this.

00:02:57.134 --> 00:02:59.512
Right, right, right. Still getting used to that.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:02.557
I have so much energy. I think it's this new plant-based diet

00:03:02.557 --> 00:03:04.767
and that I don't have to chase you anymore.

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:06.643
I'm just like, aah!

00:03:06.643 --> 00:03:08.729
Hm. Have you tried jogging?

00:03:08.729 --> 00:03:10.981
What's jogging? It's running

00:03:10.981 --> 00:03:13.817
without a terrified animal in front of you.

00:03:13.817 --> 00:03:17.029
Think that'll work? I'm desperately hoping so.

00:03:20.116 --> 00:03:21.867
There you go, sweeties.

00:03:21.867 --> 00:03:24.036
[SLURPING] [LAUGHS]

00:03:24.036 --> 00:03:25.204
Hey.

00:03:26.872 --> 00:03:29.833
I can't believe this might actually turn into something.

00:03:36.048 --> 00:03:37.258
[PHONE RINGING]

00:03:37.258 --> 00:03:38.468
THOMAS: I'll get it!

00:03:38.468 --> 00:03:39.594
[SIGHS]

00:03:39.594 --> 00:03:41.554
BEA: It might be the publisher!

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:44.474
Peter, you know not to touch this stuff.

00:03:44.474 --> 00:03:47.810
Honestly, my kids will be so much better behaved.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:49.604
Hm. Hello?

00:03:49.604 --> 00:03:51.564
[♪♪♪]

00:03:53.899 --> 00:03:55.610
Miss you, Dad.

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:58.862
No one gets me the way you did.

00:03:58.862 --> 00:04:01.031
Bea, Bea, it is. It's the publisher.

00:04:01.031 --> 00:04:03.826
[TOMMY GRUNTING SOFTLY]

00:04:03.826 --> 00:04:05.244
BEA: Hello. Ah!

00:04:06.912 --> 00:04:08.080
BEA: Yes, this is she.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:09.624
[SNIFFING]

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:13.169
No! Tommy!

00:04:13.169 --> 00:04:15.254
Those are Mr. McGregor's.

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:18.215
Well, but you used to steal from him all the time.

00:04:18.215 --> 00:04:19.883
We share the garden now.

00:04:19.883 --> 00:04:23.554
Oh, because he married the lady, you do what he says now?

00:04:23.554 --> 00:04:25.181
No, not because of that.

00:04:25.181 --> 00:04:27.016
Well, kind of because of that. It's...

00:04:27.016 --> 00:04:29.684
Look, just don't touch the tomatoes, badger.

00:04:29.684 --> 00:04:32.146
Oh, okay. Ah-ah-ah-ah-ah!

00:04:32.146 --> 00:04:34.106
[GROANS]

00:04:34.106 --> 00:04:35.399
Ah.

00:04:35.399 --> 00:04:36.359
[GRUNTS]

00:04:36.359 --> 00:04:37.985
Ah. Ugh.

00:04:37.985 --> 00:04:40.279
Uh... Ah...

00:04:40.279 --> 00:04:42.781
Uh? Ah? Um...

00:04:42.781 --> 00:04:45.326
And? Oh, ugh!

00:04:45.326 --> 00:04:47.203
[GROANING]

00:04:47.203 --> 00:04:48.871
I swear, if it wasn't for me...

00:04:48.871 --> 00:04:52.583
Thank you. Oh, you're very... You're very kind.

00:04:52.583 --> 00:04:56.128
Mm-hm. The 11:15 train to Gloucester?

00:04:56.128 --> 00:04:57.963
Yeah, we should be able to make that.

00:04:57.963 --> 00:04:59.882
[GASPS] [GASPS]

00:04:59.882 --> 00:05:03.302
I knew it! I saw you! Ugh!

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:05.846
Get out! Get out of my garden! Oh! Huh?

00:05:05.846 --> 00:05:07.431
The rabbits would love to come.

00:05:07.431 --> 00:05:08.974
It'd be such a fun adventure.

00:05:08.974 --> 00:05:10.434
I knew you wouldn't change.

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:12.061
You're the same naughty rabbit...

00:05:12.061 --> 00:05:13.770
Thanks. Bye. ...you've always been!

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:18.234
Just leave my tomatoes alone! You have everything else!

00:05:21.571 --> 00:05:24.073
See? I've told him a million times.

00:05:24.073 --> 00:05:26.576
He doesn't listen to me. Go easy on him.

00:05:26.576 --> 00:05:29.870
He's getting used to the idea that you're here to stay.

00:05:31.746 --> 00:05:32.789
[SIGHS]

00:05:32.789 --> 00:05:35.000
[♪♪♪]

00:05:36.335 --> 00:05:37.503
Huh?

00:05:40.423 --> 00:05:41.756
Huh?

00:05:41.756 --> 00:05:44.759
Yeah. You can use your front legs too.

00:05:44.759 --> 00:05:46.761
Oh, right, right, right, right, right.

00:05:46.761 --> 00:05:48.347
[GRUNTING SOFTLY]

00:05:50.057 --> 00:05:51.601
[SIGHS]

00:05:51.601 --> 00:05:53.143
[TRAIN HORN BLOWS]

00:05:53.143 --> 00:05:55.354
[♪♪♪]

00:05:56.731 --> 00:05:58.274
[ALL GASPING]

00:05:58.274 --> 00:06:01.776
Wow, is this all for us? That's what the ticket said.

00:06:01.776 --> 00:06:04.071
Only the best for the next big thing.

00:06:04.071 --> 00:06:06.073
BEA: Oh, what do we have here?

00:06:06.073 --> 00:06:08.325
[RABBITS LAUGHING, GRUNTING EXCITEDLY]

00:06:09.452 --> 00:06:10.578
Hm?

00:06:10.578 --> 00:06:12.246
[SNIFFS]

00:06:12.246 --> 00:06:13.623
[GASPS]

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:16.791
[GASPS EXCITEDLY]

00:06:16.791 --> 00:06:18.628
[SQUEALS, LAUGHS]

00:06:18.628 --> 00:06:21.213
BEA: "Enjoy the journey. It's just the beginning."

00:06:21.213 --> 00:06:24.675
A bit presumptuous, isn't it?

00:06:24.675 --> 00:06:27.595
"Forgive me for being presumptuous."

00:06:27.595 --> 00:06:29.722
He's good. Hm.

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:32.683
As someone who's been on a train before, a few pointers.

00:06:32.683 --> 00:06:34.602
Don't stare at the scenery rushing by.

00:06:34.602 --> 00:06:36.312
Look at a fixed point on the horizon

00:06:36.312 --> 00:06:38.230
and just lock your eyes onto that.

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:40.232
[FLOPSY & MOPSY GROAN]

00:06:40.232 --> 00:06:41.858
Mm? Oh.

00:06:41.858 --> 00:06:43.902
[FLOPSY & MOPSY GROANING]

00:06:43.902 --> 00:06:45.946
You okay?

00:06:45.946 --> 00:06:48.449
When you're on a train, the best thing is to look

00:06:48.449 --> 00:06:50.951
at a fixed point on the horizon.

00:06:50.951 --> 00:06:53.496
[BOTH GRUNTING]

00:06:53.496 --> 00:06:55.038
[MUNCHING LOUDLY]

00:06:57.249 --> 00:06:59.001
Oh, no. Ha-ha-ha!

00:06:59.001 --> 00:07:02.045
Oh! Magic, magic, magic.

00:07:02.045 --> 00:07:03.464
Magic!

00:07:03.464 --> 00:07:06.925
Oh, no. Cotton-Tail just discovered sugar.

00:07:06.925 --> 00:07:09.595
Hey, we had a good run.

00:07:09.595 --> 00:07:11.888
Ha-ha! "Lavatory."

00:07:11.888 --> 00:07:13.683
[LAUGHING]

